I had a priest character who was doing rather well (+7 mace), when he
encountered an orc-captain with poison arrows.  Some projectile fun ensued,
and whenever the captain shot arrows at me (which by the way happened twice
every turn... very annoying.  I can't shoot two arrows per turn; why should he
be able to?), I got the message:

The orc-captain shoots a poisoned black arrow.  You are almost hit by a
poisoned black arrow!  The poison didn't seem to harm you.

twice.  I went away, because I didn't have the HP to fight him, and returned
later... blind but esp.  He fired before I could close with him:

It misses.  The poison was deadly...--More--
The "It misses" was definitely the cap'n's arrow, as there was nobody else
around.

I was toast.  Is this a bug? (rhetorical question)

